<div style=3D"direction: ltr;">This message is a notice.<br>
<br>
The Oregon Parks and Recreation Department record is now complete at https:=
//oprdvolunteerabuse.org/accountability/oprd<br>
<br>
It contains 199 documents. Every letter I sent and every response I receive=
d is posted in date order, as a PDF and as the unmodified original email fi=
le as it was sent or received.<br>
<br>
You are referred to by role. Park Supervisor. Park Manager. Volunteer Servi=
ces Lead. Program Manager. Your names do not appear in any page, heading, c=
aption, or description I have written, in any part of the archive. I remove=
d them, and they will not be restored.
 This means search engines and other archiving tools will not archive your =
names as part of this project, and if any have previously, they will natura=
lly update on their independent schedules.<br>
<br>
That is a choice about emphasis. What happened in that park was very seriou=
s, but it went well beyond you, and your part belongs in the record as what=
 it was, inside something that grew through every level above you that touc=
hed it. Emphasizing your actions
 at this point would deemphasize the larger pattern I documented, and thus =
the archive chooses not to bear your names forward.</div>
